Verifier type modifiers and SYSCALL helpers (4.19 backport)
========================================================

Reference: local android-5.15-mainline. No defconfig changes are required by
this patch. Enable the usual BPF syscall/JIT/tracing options in menuconfig.
The tracing helper set remains subject to CONFIG options, capabilities, GPL,
helper .allowed callbacks and verifier map/program restrictions from 5.15.
"Full helper support" does not mean bypassing these restrictions.

Host regression checks (do not load the verifier or exercise SMP scheduling):

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf/test_helper_type_modifiers.py
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf/test_modifier_compatibility.py
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf/test_helper_memory_modifiers.py
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf/test_sleepable_migration.py
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf/test_callback_reference_scope.py
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf/test_arm64_callback_tail.py
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf/test_arm64_trampoline.py

Device regression:

Export this tree's UAPI with `make ARCH=arm64 headers_install
INSTALL_HDR_PATH=/tmp/gauguin-uapi`, then build syscall_helpers_user.c using
an Android ARM64 compiler and -I/tmp/gauguin-uapi/include. Run as root:

  /data/local/tmp/syscall_helpers_user 10000

It loads a BPF_PROG_TYPE_SYSCALL | BPF_F_SLEEPABLE program without libbpf,
faults user pages with copy_from_user, compares CPU numbers across the helper,
and exercises sys_bpf(MAP_CREATE) and sys_close. It creates and closes only
its own temporary maps. Run under scheduler load and concurrent taskset
changes for affinity stress. Repeat after the device has been idle and after
several minutes of uptime. CPU hotplug/isolation stress must be tested on the
actual Qualcomm kernel; the host migration test uses scheduler stubs.

helper_readonly.c provides positive and negative BPF objects. The normal
object passes read-only map data to strtol; -DBAD_WRITE attempts to use that
data as get_current_comm output and must fail verifier load. Use a modern
libbpf loader that sets the rodata map BPF_F_RDONLY_PROG and freezes it.
Compiling either object does not prove the verifier result.

Migration dependency:

migrate_disable/enable now preserve CPU locality while allowing preemption
and sleeping, including nested calls. Requested affinity (cpus_allowed) is
separate from effective affinity (cpus_ptr). Concurrent affinity changes use
the 5.15 pending-completion mechanism; scheduler placement, balancing and
Qualcomm isolation honor pinned tasks. CPU deactivation drains nr_pinned
before stop_machine, with a sleeping poll to avoid taking wakeup locks from
instrumentation under rq->lock. Long-running sleepable BPF programs can
therefore delay CPU offlining. They are not given a new runtime timeout.
